 my chains,"},{"verse":11,"text":"who once was useless to you, but now is useful to you and to me."},{"verse":12,"text":"I am sending him back. Therefore receive him, that is, my own heart,"},{"verse":13,"text":"whom I desired to keep with me, that on your behalf he might serve me in my chains for the Good News."},{"verse":14,"text":"But I was willing to do nothing without your consent, that your goodness would not be as of necessity, but of free will."},{"verse":15,"text":"For perhaps he was therefore separated from you for a while that you would have him forever,"},{"verse":16,"text":"no longer as a slave, but more than a slave, a beloved brother—especially to me, but how much rather to you, both in the flesh and in the Lord."},{"verse":17,"text":"If then you count me a partner, receive him as you would receive me."},{"verse":18,"text":"But if he has wronged you at all or owes you anything, put that to my account."},{"verse":19,"text":"I, Paul, write this with my own hand: I will repay it (not to mention to you that you owe to me even your own self besides)."},{"verse":20,"text":"Yes, brother, let me have joy from you in the Lord. Refresh my heart in the Lord."},{"verse":21,"text":"Having confidence in your obedience, I write to you, knowing that you will do even beyond what I say."},{"verse":22,"text":"Also, prepare a guest room for me, for I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you."},{"verse":23,"text":"Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, greets you,"},{"verse":24,"text":"as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers."},{"verse":25,"text":"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen."}],"hasArtwork":false,"availableLangs":[]}]